            <div class="probate-intro">
        	<p class="leasing-tips__lead">    
				<p>Probate gives legal authority to an executor named in a will, allowing them to administer and distribute 
                the estate in accordance with the will. This process protects beneficiaries, honours the deceased person’s wishes, 
                and ensures assets are handled according to NSW Law. When searching for what is probate in NSW, most people want 
                to understand the purpose of the process and what it requires.</p>
