					<h3>Legal Definition of Probate</h3>
					<p>Probate refers to the formal approval of a will by the Supreme Court of NSW. When people ask what is probate, 
                    they are referring to the legal process that confirms a will is valid and confirms the executor’s appointment. 
                    A Grant of Probate gives the executor authority to administer the estate of the deceased person.</p>
